{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792923602,"nonce":"95r/5v0HVZMQBI8Nx3pbi/UDWSU=","title":"LSP: Lua, Python and frontend languages in caribou-lsp","message":"Part of 1626b90d930d209e848220743e00494408af449d2cdabdddea70f6c0a5337545 (caribou lsp).\n\nZyntax's Python and Lua frontends have no editor support. They parse to a\nTypedProgram or stop at the first error, which carries a byte span (Python:\nSyntax, Unsupported or Library; Lua adds Rejected and Annotation).\nSourceMap in typed_ast turns spans into lines and columns.\n\n- **Diagnostics.** Parse each open document through its frontend and report\n  its error with the span.\n- **Cross-language imports.** Resolve imports of other languages' modules\n  through the registry. For Python, that is a HostResolver answering\n  HostModule from the module's interface. A module Caribou provides is\n  then never \"not found\".\n- **Navigation.** Hover and definition at a use of another language's class\n  or function, from its interface and its source path.\n- **Frontend languages.** A Zyntax language whose grammar is a frontend file\n  in the sources gets the same, through caribou_zyntax.\n- **One error per file.** Each frontend stops at its first error. Reporting\n  more needs Zyntax's frontends to recover, which is Zyntax's work.","files":null}]}